<title>USA: Shell says U.S. Capline nominations for Oct down.</title>
<headline>Shell says U.S. Capline nominations for Oct down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil said that October pipeline nominations on Capline, a large crude oil artery linking the Gulf Coast with the Midwest, were slightly down compared with the previous month.</p>
<p>Nominations for October were 1,001,209 barrels per day (bpd), about 23,316 bpd less than September throughput.</p>
<p>Actual throughput for September was 1,024,525 bpd.</p>
<p>The drop in nominations was attributed to seasonal falls in Midwest demand, and autumn refinery turnarounds.</p>
<p>Capline can carry from 1.1 million to 1.2 million bpd, and is a major pipeline into the landlocked Midwest.</p>
<p>Shell Oil is the operator of Capline and is part of the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
<p>--Jacqueline Wong, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
